// Worked example 2: the Parcel tracker project, described in parcel-tracker.md.
// A draft for human review: every line comes from a file named in parcel-tracker.md.

model parcels: Parcel tracker
  > Couriers scan parcels; recipients get a text at each step and can check where their
    parcel is.

audiences exec "Executive", manager "Manager" (default), engineer "Engineer" (code)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- elements

courier: Courier | Scans parcels on the road [person]
  > Scans each parcel when it is picked up, moved and delivered.

recipient: Recipient | Waits for a parcel [person]
  > Gets a text message at each step and can open the tracking page.

tracker: Parcel tracker | Follows every parcel from pickup to door [system]
  > A mobile app for couriers and three back-end parts, joined by an event queue.
  @exec: | Tells customers where their parcel is
  @engineer >> An npm workspaces monorepo. `deploy/compose.yaml` runs `tracking-api`,
    `notifier`, `nats` and `postgres`; the courier app ships through the app stores.

  scan-app: Courier app | Scans parcel labels [service package]
    icon monitor
    > The phone app couriers use to scan labels and mark deliveries.
    @engineer: | packages/scan-app, React Native
    @engineer >> Sends each scan to `TRACKING_API_URL`, keeping scans on the phone while there
      is no signal.

  tracking-api: Tracking API | Takes scans, answers status questions [service package]
    icon api
    > Records every scan and tells recipients where their parcel is.
    @exec: Tracking service | Knows where every parcel is
    @engineer: | packages/tracking-api, Fastify :8080

    scan-intake: Scan intake | Records scans [module]
      @engineer: | src/routes/scans.ts
      @engineer >> `POST /scans`. Saves the scan, then publishes `parcel.scanned` on NATS.

    status-lookup: Status lookup | Answers where a parcel is [module]
      @engineer: | src/routes/status.ts
      @engineer >> `GET /parcels/:code`, the page behind the link in each text message.

  events: Parcel events | Every scan, in order [queue]
    icon refresh
    > Passes news of each scan from the tracking API to the notifier.
    @engineer: | NATS JetStream, stream PARCELS
    @engineer >> The `nats` service in `deploy/compose.yaml`, run with `-js`.

  notifier: Notifier | Texts recipients [service package]
    icon gear
    > Turns each scan into a short text message for the recipient.
    @engineer: | packages/notifier, Node worker
    @engineer >> A durable consumer of `parcel.scanned`. Message wording lives in
      `src/templates/`.

  shared-events: Event formats | What a scan event looks like [module package]
    icon grid
    > The one definition of a scan event, shared so both sides agree.
    @engineer: | packages/shared-events
    @engineer >> Zod schemas and the TypeScript types made from them.

  db: Tracking database | Every parcel and scan [store]
    @engineer: | PostgreSQL 16, database tracking

// Unsure: the README says texts are sent "through our SMS partner" without naming it.
sms: SMS gateway | Sends text messages [external]
  @engineer: | HTTPS API, key in SMS_API_KEY

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- relationships

courier scans parcels with scan-app
recipient checks a parcel with status-lookup
scan-app sends scans to scan-intake
  @engineer: POSTs /scans to
scan-intake saves scans in db
  @engineer: INSERTs scans into
scan-intake publishes scan events to events
  @engineer: publishes parcel.scanned to
notifier takes scan events from events
  @engineer: consumes parcel.scanned from
notifier sends texts through sms
sms delivers texts to recipient
status-lookup reads parcel history from db

tracking-api depends on shared-events [code]
notifier depends on shared-events [code]

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- views

view big-picture: Big picture
  show courier, recipient, tracker +1, sms

view services: Services
  show courier, recipient, tracker +2, sms
  > Every part, with the tracking API opened up.

view engineering: Engineering: packages
  show [package]
  kind code
  @exec: How the code is organised

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- scenarios

scenario parcel-scanned: A parcel is scanned
  > From a courier's scan to the recipient's text message.
  courier scans a parcel with scan-app
  scan-app sends the scan to scan-intake
  scan-intake saves the scan in db
  scan-intake publishes a scan event to events
  notifier takes the scan event from events
  notifier sends a text through sms
  sms delivers the text to recipient
    > The text holds a link to the tracking page.

scenario status-check: A recipient checks a parcel
  recipient opens the tracking link with status-lookup
  status-lookup reads the parcel's history from db
  db returns the history to status-lookup
  status-lookup shows where the parcel is to recipient

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- walkthrough

walkthrough tour: A tour of the Parcel tracker
  step big-picture
    > Couriers scan, recipients get texts. In between is the Parcel tracker.
  step big-picture: events
    > The parts never call each other directly to send texts: each scan becomes an
      **event**, and the notifier picks it up.
    @exec > Scans and texts are decoupled, so a slow text service never slows couriers down.
  step parcel-scanned: 1-4
    > A scan is saved first, then announced.
  step parcel-scanned: 5-7
    > The notifier turns the announcement into a text.
  step services: status-lookup
    > The text links to **Status lookup**, inside the tracking API.
  step status-check
    > The recipient sees where their parcel is.
  step engineering
    for engineer
    > The tracking API and the notifier share one package of event formats.
